## 🔌 API Client

The API client ([data/api/api-client.ts](file:///e:/NextProjects/Deals-Dashboard/data/api/api-client.ts)) provides:
- **HTTP Methods**: GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE
- **Bearer Token Authentication**
- **Automatic 401 Interception** → triggers auth modal
- **FormData Support** for file uploads
- **Comprehensive Logging**

```typescript
class ApiClient {
  async get<T>(endpoint, queryParams?): Promise<T>
  async post<T>(endpoint, data): Promise<T>
  async put<T>(endpoint, data): Promise<T>
  async patch<T>(endpoint, data): Promise<T>
  async delete<T>(endpoint, data?): Promise<T>
}
```

---

## 🔐 Authentication System

### Flow Diagram
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant LF as Login Form
    participant AS as AuthService
    participant AR as AuthRepository
    participant API as API Client
    participant TS as TokenStorage
    participant MW as Middleware

    U->>LF: Enter credentials
    LF->>AS: login(credentials)
    AS->>AR: login(credentials)
    AR->>API: POST /admins/login
    API-->>AR: { token, admin }
    AR->>TS: setToken(token)
    AR-->>LF: AuthResponse
    LF->>U: Redirect to /dashboard/users
    
    Note over MW: Subsequent requests
    MW->>TS: Check auth_token cookie
    alt Valid Token
        MW-->>U: Allow access
    else No Token
        MW-->>U: Redirect to /login
    end
```

### Token Storage
- **localStorage**: Stores `auth_token` for API requests
- **Cookie**: `auth_token` cookie for middleware SSR auth
- **Expiry**: 7 days

### Role-Based Access
- **Super Admin**: Full access including `/dashboard/admins`
- **Regular Admin**: Limited access (no admin management)

